### Google Register Test (Authorization Code Flow)
POST {{Web_HostAddress}}/api/Users/GoogleRegister
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "authorizationCode": "your-google-authorization-code-here",
  "redirectUri": "http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback"
}

### Google Register for Mobile/SPA (without cookies)
POST {{Web_HostAddress}}/api/Users/GoogleRegister?useCookies=false
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "authorizationCode": "your-google-authorization-code-here",
  "redirectUri": "http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback"
}

### Google Register with Lecturer Role
POST {{Web_HostAddress}}/api/Users/GoogleRegister
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": "your-google-id-token-here",
  "role": "Lecturer"
}

### Google Register without Role (defaults to User)
POST {{Web_HostAddress}}/api/Users/GoogleRegister
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": ""
}

### Response should be:
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "data": {
#     "token": {
#       "accessToken": "jwt-access-token",
#       "refreshToken": "refresh-token",
#       "expireMin": 360000
#     },
#     "isNewUser": true,
#     "userInfo": {
#       "id": "google-user-id",
#       "email": "user@gmail.com",
#       "name": "User Name",
#       "givenName": "User",
#       "familyName": "Name",
#       "picture": "https://...",
#       "emailVerified": true
#     }
#   }
# }

### Notes:
# 1. Replace "your-google-authorization-code-here" with actual Google authorization code
# 2. The authorization code is obtained from Google OAuth flow with response_type=code
# 3. The redirectUri must match exactly what was used in the OAuth flow
# 4. Backend will exchange the code for access token and get user info
# 5. If user already exists, isNewUser will be false
# 6. New users will have no role by default
# 7. Use ?useCookies=false for mobile/SPA applications
# 8. Role parameter is optional, defaults to "User"
# 9. Valid roles: "User", "Administrator", "Lecturer" 